<!--
  ILLink substitutions for the NativeAOT Release publish only (PenBridge.Mac.csproj, issue #42).

  Foundation.NSObject's static constructor has one private static field per Apple framework
  (`fl`, `al`, `ab`, `wl`, ...), each initialized with ObjCRuntime.Dlfcn.dlopen(string, int). They
  exist so a dynamically registered, untrimmed app finds every framework's classes. NativeAOT uses the
  static registrar and full trimming, and the SDK links every framework whose types survive trimming
  (LC_LOAD_DYLIB), so this preload is redundant. It still maps ~45 frameworks (WebKit, MapKit, GameKit,
  SwiftUI, ...) and ~600 images into the process: about 28 MB of resident (shared) pages at idle.

  The public dlopen(string, int) overload is stubbed (returns IntPtr.Zero); nothing else changes.
  Invariant this relies on: in the trimmed Microsoft.macOS.dll the only callers of that overload are
  NSObject's framework fields, whose values are never read. Libraries.*.Handle (field and constant
  lookups) and Dlfcn.dlopen(string, Dlfcn.Mode) go through the internal _dlopen and are unaffected.
  Guarded automatically: scripts/check-bundle.sh with the Release flag (CI) runs
  scripts/lib/check-aot-substitutions.cs on obj/Release/net10.0-macos/<rid>/linked/Microsoft.macOS.dll
  and fails if the stub is missing, a caller is outside NSObject's .cctor, a result is not stored
  straight into an NSObject field, or any of those fields is read.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Microsoft.macOS">
    <type fullname="ObjCRuntime.Dlfcn">
      <method signature="System.IntPtr dlopen(System.String,System.Int32)" body="stub" />
    </type>
  </assembly>
</linker>
